Table Accounts has these rows (acc_id, branch, balance): (101, Pune, 72000), (102, Delhi, 45000), (103, Pune, 51000), (104, Delhi, 90000), (105, Agra, 60000), (106, Delhi, 55000), (107, Pune, 30000), (108, Agra, 20000).

Which branches does this query return?

SELECT branch, COUNT(*) FROM Accounts WHERE balance > 50000 GROUP BY branch HAVING COUNT(*) >= 2;
